2. Design System Rules
A. Visual Simplification
Reduce Internal Detail: Strip unnecessary inner line work when switching from desktop to mobile views.
Filled vs. Outlined:
Desktop: Outlined styles are common for lightweight density.
Mobile: Use Filled variants for active states and critical navigation to maximize visual tap confirmation.
B. Ergonomics & Placement
Thumb Zone Rule (Mobile): Primary action icons (Navigation, Search, Actions) must live in the lower 60% of the mobile viewport.
Top-Bar Offloading (Desktop): Secondary or utility icons (Settings, Profile, Export) belong in upper corners or sidebars.
C. Interaction & Feedback
Hover Elimination: Never hide essential icon labels behind hover tooltips on mobile. Provide explicit micro-labels or visible context.
Touch Feedback: Always pair :active states with scaling or opacity drops (e.g., transform: scale(0.95)) for instantaneous tactile response.
3. Production CSS Implementation
Use this utility pattern to automatically handle touch targets, spacing, and interaction states responsively:
/* Base Icon Button Container */
.icon-btn {
  /* Common layout defaults */
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  border: none;
  background: transparent;
  cursor: pointer;
  user-select: none;
  -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
  
  /* Desktop sizing (default) */
  min-width: 32px;
  min-height: 32px;
  padding: 4px;
  gap: 6px;
  transition: background-color 0.15s ease, transform 0.1s ease;
}

/* Embedded SVG styling */
.icon-btn svg {
  width: 20px;
  height: 20px;
  stroke-width: 1.5px;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* Desktop Hover State */
@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
  .icon-btn:hover {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
}

/* Mobile Adaptation via Media Queries */
@media (pointer: coarse) and (hover: none) {
  .icon-btn {
    /* Touch target expansion */
    min-width: 48px;
    min-height: 48px;
    padding: 8px;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .icon-btn svg {
    /* Visible asset enlargement & bolder stroke */
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    stroke-width: 2px;
  }

  /* Immediate feedback for touch press */
  .icon-btn:active {
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
    transform: scale(0.94);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
}


4. Adaptation Checklist
[ ] Touch Target: Are all mobile icon buttons extended to at least 44x44px or 48x48px?
[ ] Labels: Are navigation icons accompanied by visible labels or clear visual contexts on touch screens?
[ ] Stroke Weight: Do icons remain clear when rendered on a low-brightness mobile screen?
[ ] Placement: Are key interactive icons positioned within easy thumb reach?
[ ] Feedback: Does tapping an icon produce immediate visual feedback (e.g., active state/scale down)?
